    "All adapter SRAM clocks currently run continuously; no low-power clock-gating claim.",
    "The generated behavior model is explicitly corrected from old-address writes to current-address writes. No transistor equivalence is inferred from changing a model.",
    "The adapter preserves held read output and vendor simultaneous read/write behavior without adding bus latency in the tested profiles.",
    "The six real SoC codec/bus tests include all addresses, bank boundaries, byte enables, foreground/background scrub contention and reset retention, but are fault-free. SEU campaigns and full formal sequential equivalence remain separate.",
    "BIST remains tied off, A_DLY high, and runtime guards reject nonuniform masks or unsupported controls.",
    "Independent macro PVT/PEX timing, Liberty, density, power, full layout integration and complete-chip LVS remain open.",
    "The first SoC parity launch used host Icarus12 and was rejected before elaboration by the existing version guard. The successful retry uses the existing OSS CAD Suite Icarus14; the guard was not weakened."
